{"post": {"ID": 466, "post_title": "10 Simple Digital Marketing Strategies That You Need to Survive", "post_excerpt": "A digital marketing strategy is a plan for reaching your goals online. How to build one in seven steps, ten strategies to choose from and how to measure results.", "post_author": "3", "post_date": "2025-01-14 21:09:04", "post_modified": "2026-11-13 06:01:35", "post_content_b64": ""}, "meta": {"_thumbnail_id": "465", "_yoast_wpseo_title": "Digital Marketing Strategies: Types, Steps | Reinforce Lab", "_yoast_wpseo_metadesc": "A digital marketing strategy is a plan for reaching your goals online. See how to build one in seven steps, plus 10 strategies to choose from.", "rl_updated": "2026-11-13", "_rl_carried": "a:3:{s:7:\"prod_id\";i:216738;s:4:\"from\";s:90:\"https://reinforcelab.com/simple-digital-marketing-strategies-that-you-need-to-survive-for/\";s:8:\"decision\";s:5:\"D-178\";}", "rl_type": "guide", "_yoast_wpseo_primary_category": "6", "rl_answer": "A digital marketing strategy is a long-term plan for how a business will reach its goals using online channels. It names the audience, the goals, the channels, the budget and owners, the content and the measures. Build one in seven steps, then review it every month.", "rl_takeaways": "A strategy is the long-term plan. A campaign is a time-limited push inside it. A tactic is one action inside a campaign.\nEvery strategy rests on six parts: audience, goals, channels, budget and owners, content, and measures.\nBuild it in seven steps: describe the customer, set goals with a number and a date, check what you do now, choose a few channels, plan content around buyer questions, set budget and owners, then measure and adjust.\nTwo or three channels done well beat seven done badly.\nSearch work takes time: Google says changes can show in hours or take months, and suggests waiting a few weeks before judging.\nTrack early signals and final results, and review them every month.", "rl_faqs": "What is a digital marketing strategy? | A digital marketing strategy is a long-term plan for how a business will reach its goals using online channels. It names the audience, the goals, the channels, the budget, the content and the measures that show whether it works.\nWhat is the difference between a digital marketing strategy and a campaign? | A strategy is the long-term plan and the reason behind it. A campaign is a time-limited push toward one goal inside that plan. For example, the strategy may be to win small clinics through search content, and one campaign may be a six-week workshop promotion.\nWhat are the main types of digital marketing strategies? | The main ones are search engine optimization, content marketing, pay-per-click advertising, social media marketing, email marketing, influencer marketing, affiliate marketing, mobile marketing, video marketing and search optimized for AI and voice. You do not need all of them.\nHow do I choose the right digital marketing strategy? | Start with your customer, not the channel. Find out where your buyers look for answers, set a goal with a number and a date, and pick two or three channels that fit both. Test, measure and adjust each month.\nHow much should I spend on digital marketing? | There is no single right figure. Your budget should cover media spend, tools, content production and staff time, and each channel should have an owner and a goal. Start with the channels that fit your buyers and increase spending only on the ones that bring results.\nHow long does a digital marketing strategy take to work? | It depends on the channel. Paid ads can bring visits quickly. For search, Google says some changes take a few hours and others several months, and suggests waiting a few weeks before judging whether a change helped. Review your numbers every month.\nHow do I measure whether my strategy works? | Track early signals, such as visits, sign-ups and replies, and final results, such as enquiries, sales and revenue. Use Google Search Console and your analytics tool, set your goals before you start, and compare before and after.\nDoes SEO still matter with AI search? | Yes. Semrush notes that the same authority and content structure that earn search rankings also shape which sites AI tools cite. Clear answers, clear authorship and consistent facts help in both.", "rl_sources": "Semrush: Digital marketing strategies, types and how to build one | https://www.semrush.com/blog/digital-marketing-strategies\nHubSpot: Digital marketing strategy playbook | https://blog.hubspot.com/marketing/marketing-2015\nContentStudio: Digital marketing strategies | https://contentstudio.io/blog/digital-marketing-strategies\nGoogle Search Central: SEO Starter Guide | https://developers.google.com/search/docs/fundamentals/seo-starter-guide\nGoogle Search Central: Creating helpful, reliable, people-first content | https://developers.google.com/search/docs/fundamentals/creating-helpful-content", "rl_g_glossary": "Strategy | The long-term plan for how a business reaches its goals.\nCampaign | A time-limited push toward one goal inside a strategy.\nTactic | One action inside a campaign, such as sending an email.\nKPI | A measure of progress toward a goal.\nCustomer profile | A written description of who buys and why. Also called a persona.", "rl_g_cta_service": "services/best-search-engine-optimization-services", "rl_g_cta_after": "5", "rl_g_cta_head": "Want your marketing and search to work together?", "rl_g_cta_sub": "Reinforce Lab builds the search side of your strategy as one system and measures it in leads and revenue.", "rl_g_cta_button": "See SEO services", "_yoast_wpseo_focuskw": "digital marketing strategies"}}